  "title": "Theranos Whistleblower Aftermath",
  "objective": "Explore ethical dilemmas and systemic pressures that allowed Theranos' fraudulent technology to persist despite early warnings.",
  "brief": "Theranos whistleblower aftermath (2015-2016). Lab technicians and employees exposed the fraudulent blood testing technology, facing legal threats and personal retaliation. Stakeholders: a lab technician running tests they know produce unreliable results who fears both patient harm and career destruction if they speak up, a hospital procurement director who integrated Theranos devices into patient workflows affecting thousands of diagnostic decisions, a patient who received incorrect blood test results that led to unnecessary medical procedures, and a Walgreens corporate partnership manager with $140M committed to the Theranos in-store testing rollout.",
